		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5053&amp;p=36727#p36727"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>I have a V2 and it works quite good , the "Click Suppression" takes away all annoying clicks.<br>The only problem I have is that some of the SVXLink repeaters here in Stockholm seems to be wider than my radio even if I select wide on the<br>radio.<br>So I notice some severe clipping on RX on received TX.<br><br>I've also seen on my deviation meter that the deviation is around 4 kHZ even in Wide setting on TX , I haven't tried yet with my signal generator <br>to feed wider signal to see if I can  reproduce what I hear on live traffic.<br><br>I have some ideas to change the software to use the widest setting on the circuit that handles FM RX so I can see if that makes any difference.<br>The IC have three different bandwidths and the widest is around 7 kHz.</div></blockquote>Okay, thank you very much for your feedback.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6826">BA7IQE</a> — Sun Apr 13, 2025 3:39 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
