		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5053&amp;p=36723#p36723"><![CDATA[
I have a V2 and it works quite good , the "Click Suppression" takes away all annoying clicks.<br>The only problem I have is that some of the SVXLink repeaters here in Stockholm seems to be wider than my radio even if I select wide on the<br>radio.<br>So I notice some severe clipping on RX on received TX.<br><br>I've also seen on my deviation meter that the deviation is around 4 kHZ even in Wide setting on TX , I haven't tried yet with my signal generator <br>to feed wider signal to see if I can  reproduce what I hear on live traffic.<br><br>I have some ideas to change the software to use the widest setting on the circuit that handles FM RX so I can see if that makes any difference.<br>The IC have three different bandwidths and the widest is around 7 kHz.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2867">SA0BUX</a> — Sat Apr 12, 2025 7:18 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
